# {{ cli_name }}

Everything command-specific is in the CLI itself — run `{{ cli_name }}`
with no arguments for version + command list, `{{ cli_name }} <command>
--help` for details. This document only covers what `--help` can't tell
you. If you can run the CLI but not read files, `{{ cli_name }} --ai`
prints this document.

## Install (if `{{ cli_name }} --version` fails)

{% set github = not repository_url or repository_url.startswith('https://github.com/') -%}
{% if not github -%}
```bash
uv tool install {{ dist_name }} --index https://homeserver.tailee01ab.ts.net:3000/api/packages/bolandeu/pypi/simple
```

From the git tag instead:

{% endif -%}
```bash
{% if repository_url -%}
uv tool install "{{ dist_name }} @ git+{{ repository_url }}.git@vX.Y.Z"
{%- else -%}
uv tool install "{{ dist_name }} @ git+https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git@vX.Y.Z"
{%- endif %}
```

Replace `vX.Y.Z` with the latest release tag (install from a tag, never a
branch: [the Standard](https://github.com/bolandeu/python-package-gate/blob/main/skills/cli-builder/reference/standard.md), Install).

Same command on macOS, Linux and Windows; `uv tool upgrade {{ dist_name }}`
updates it. Do not run from source unless asked to develop the CLI.

{% if github -%}
The repository may be private. On an auth error (`Authentication failed`,
`could not read Username`, `Repository not found`) do not ask for a token:
run `gh auth status`; if it passes, `gh auth setup-git` and retry; if not,
ask the user to run `gh auth login`. With SSH keys configured, this works
without any of that:

```bash
{% if repository_url -%}
uv tool install "{{ dist_name }} @ git+ssh://git@github.com/{{ repository_url | replace('https://github.com/', '') }}.git@vX.Y.Z"
{%- else -%}
uv tool install "{{ dist_name }} @ git+ssh://git@github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git@vX.Y.Z"
{%- endif %}
```

{% endif -%}
## Conventions

- **`--json` on every command.** Parse stdout; never scrape human output.
  stdout is data only, stderr is diagnostics.
{%- if include_project %}
- **Project-aware.** Commands find the project by walking up from the
  current directory, or take `--project PATH`. Not initialized →
  `{{ cli_name }} init --non-interactive`.
{%- endif %}
- **`--non-interactive`** on anything that could prompt. It fails with a
  structured error instead of hanging.
{%- if include_auth %}
- **Credentials** live in the OS keychain or env vars
  (`{{ cli_name | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_<PROVIDER>_<FIELD>`), never in arguments or
  config. `auth status --check --json` reports every provider (source,
  status, expiry, quota — never values; exit 3 if a required one isn't
  ok); log in with `auth login`; never ask the user to paste a secret into
  a command line.
{%- endif %}
- **Destructive commands** are the ones whose `--help` shows `--dry-run`
  and `--confirm`. Always: run with `--dry-run`, show the user, get
  explicit sign-off, then `--confirm --non-interactive`. Never chain
  straight to `--confirm` without a human having seen the dry-run.
{%- if include_db %}
- **Data** lives in the shared PostgreSQL when `{{ cli_name | upper | regex_replace('[^A-Z0-9]', '_') }}_DATABASE_URL` is
  set (else a local SQLite file). `DATABASE_UNAVAILABLE` (exit 5) — the
  server is unreachable, nothing was written anywhere; `DATABASE_NOT_MIGRATED`
  → `{{ cli_name }} db upgrade` (changes the shared base: ask the user
  first); `db status --json` shows the revision. `db push --dry-run`
  then `db push` sends new local rows to production — run by the
  user; an agent gives the user the exact command
  (`{{ cli_name | upper | regex_replace('[^A-Z0-9]', '_') }}_PROD_DATABASE_URL`; already-present ones are skipped). Reading this tool's data
  from SQL: only the `{{ cli_name | regex_replace('[^a-z0-9]', '_') }}_v1_*` views.
{%- endif %}
- **`doctor --json`** first when something looks off — it reports
  what the CLI needs to run: its version{% if include_project %}, the project, its config{% endif %}{% if include_auth %},
  credential readiness{% endif %}{% if include_db %}, the database{% endif %} and the external programs.
{%- if include_describe %}
- **`describe --json`** — the whole CLI as one machine-readable OpenCLI
  document (commands, options, exit codes, env vars, data): the bare
  document, no `{"ok": ...}` envelope.
{%- endif %}

## Errors

Error envelope: `{"ok": false, "error": {"code", "message", "action"}}`.
Read exit code → `error.code` → `error.action` (the concrete next command).

    0  ok
    1  general (UNEXPECTED = a bug: re-run with --verbose, report; ABORTED = user said no)
    2  invalid arguments
    3  auth required{% if include_auth %}          → {{ cli_name }} auth login{% endif %}
    4  project not initialized{% if include_project %} → {{ cli_name }} init{% endif %}
    5  provider error (network / external service; already retried) → retry later
    6  CLI too old for this project → uv tool upgrade {{ dist_name }}

Only exit 5 is worth an automatic retry.
